{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ gis education teaching learning maps)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1022347074#0_2050413175","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3067","rank":1,"snippet":"1687.000000 , \"headings\": \"Schools Schools Teaching During Disruption Student “Maptivists” Inspire Invigorating STEM Curriculum GIS supports STEM in Hawaii Campus Sustainability Investing in Schools and Kids Offerings for Schools We are committed to helping schools thrive with free online mapping tools, curriculum, and support. Curriculum Solutions Free Software for Instruction Teacher Support Support for Administrators Events and webinars Community Let's Talk \" , \"segment\": \"<cover>GIS for Schools | Interactive Web Maps for K-12 Subject Matter Education Menu Overview Our Story Instructional Resources Schools Mapping Software Bundle Educator Support Higher Education Lifelong Learning Licensing Licensing Schools Lessons resonate longer when interactive web maps support K–12 subject matter. See offers Mapping Hour Teaching </cover>During Disruption ArcGIS Online supports rich lessons and projects, even in disruptions. Teachers and parents can help kids learn, on any connected device. Learn ways to teach with GIS Student “Maptivists” Inspire STEM magnet school students inspired by Will.i.am show how they used ArcGIS to understand and change their neighborhood in Boyle Heights, East L.A.. Watch video Invigorating STEM Curriculum GIS supports STEM learning with integrative, project-based experiences, providing context to education. "}}
