{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_32828322#8_68556814","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the dedicated AP Human Geography classroom page on maps and spatial thinking. It directly states that maps organize and display geographic information, make patterns and relationships apparent, support spatial thinking and problem solving, and are used to learn content and 'think through maps.' It is repeated evidence from the same source as the previous result but still directly relevant.","learned":"Maps can shape pedagogy by enabling students to think through spatial representations, learn geography content, practice problem-solving, and critically interpret maps as contextual texts."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3072","reason":"The current result list is producing highly relevant classroom evidence on maps, spatial thinking, and learning; continue to find additional grade-3 or related results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3072"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1435566299#1_3074894720","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3072","rank":3,"snippet":"address the spatial thinking abilities of young children and developmental appropriateness. The collection is not intended to be a complete map skill program, and the activities can be adapted for higher or lower grades. Click here for a downloadable summary of all activities and the learning objectives and spatial thinking concepts targeted in each activity. Mapping Concepts and Skills Spatial Thinking Learn more about the development of concepts and skills across the early years. Activity Summary Click here for a downloadable summary of all activities in the Map Skills for Elementary <cover>Students collection and the learning objectives and spatial thinking concepts targeted in each activity. Large-Format Maps</cover>State Tabletop Maps Dive into state geography learning with printable, tiled tabletop maps. World Map for Kids National Geographic's The World for Kids wall map is an enticing and engaging world map perfect for classroom, home or library. Recommended by geography educators for ages 7-12, this map features an optimized map design for readability and easy, intuitive learning. Maps of Familiar Places Introduce young students to the concept of maps as representations of places with these community maps. Park Map Introduce young students to the concept of maps as representations "}}
