{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_852272057#5_1490905620","relevance":3,"reason":"This document is dedicated to mindmapping as a brainstorming/instructional exercise and directly supports the information need by explaining that concept/cognitive maps spatially represent students' ideas and interrelationships in memory, support cooperative learning and critical thinking, and function as a constructivist instructional tool. It repeats evidence very similar to the previous result but remains directly relevant.","learned":"Mindmapping can impact pedagogy by externalizing students' cognitive structures, supporting critical thinking and cooperative learning, and facilitating problem-solving through constructivist instruction."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3072","reason":"The maps/spatial-thinking query continues to produce grade-3 evidence across classroom mapping, spatial thinking, GIS, and concept/mind mapping, so continue while it remains productive."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3072"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_722368589#7_1693271438","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3072","rank":12,"snippet":"for each food drop along the Iditarod Trail according to a race plan and run/rest schedule determined by an Iditarod musher. Standard’s Addressed: ( Local, State, or National) 1) Use a model to explain cellular respiration as a chemical process whereby the bonds of food molecules and oxygen molecules are broken and bonds in new compounds are formed that result in a net transfer of energy. 2) Show how the ideas and themes of science can be used to make real-life decisions about use of resources. 3) Use <cover>maps and other geographic representations, geospatial technologies, and spatial thinking to understand and communicate information. 4) Create equations that describe numbers or relationships. Learning Objectives: 1) Students </cover>can collaborate to brainstorm and develop questions to answer for the sake of creating an Iditarod nutrition plan (goal is to develop a standard list of questions for all students to use.)\" , \"start_char\": 2965.000000 , \"title\": \"Importance of Nutrition: Fuel for the Fire – Iditarod Nutrition Plan by Sid Lucas – Iditarod\" , \"url\": \"https://iditarod.com/edu/fuel-for-the-fire-iditarod-nutrition-plan/\" }"}}
