{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_722368589#7_1693271438","relevance":2,"reason":"This lesson plan includes a direct learning standard about using maps, geospatial technologies, and spatial thinking to understand and communicate information, but the document is mainly about an Iditarod nutrition/science activity rather than dedicated to how maps impact pedagogy.","learned":"Maps can be integrated into interdisciplinary lessons as tools for understanding and communicating information, but broad standards mentions may be secondary rather than central evidence."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"map skills\" students learning spatial thinking)","reason":"Search more directly for documents dedicated to map skills, student learning, and spatial thinking, which has been the most productive evidence pattern for grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"map skills\" students learning spatial thinking)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1435566299#0_3074892110","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3073","rank":1,"snippet":"in math and science. Young students also enhance their language skills as they collaborate and communicate about spatial relationships. Students who develop robust spatial thinking skills will be at an advantage in our increasingly global and technological society. This collection can help you teach an assortment of map skills through activities that address the spatial thinking abilities of young children and developmental appropriateness. The collection is not intended to be a complete map skill program, and the activities can be adapted for higher or lower grades. Click here for a downloadable summary of all activities and the learning objectives and spatial thinking concepts targeted in each activity. Mapping Concepts and Skills Spatial Thinking Learn more about the development of concepts and skills across the early years. Activity Summary Click here for a downloadable summary of all activities in the <cover>Map Skills for Elementary Students collection and the learning objectives and spatial thinking </cover>concepts targeted in each activity.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Map Skills for Elementary Students | National Geographic Society\" , \"url\": \"https://www.nationalgeographic.org/education/map-skills-elementary-students/\" }"}}
